items.text:
I wrote this in Feb. It's more true now than ever. 

As the labs absorb the scaffolding that used to wrap the model, any product that's just generic reasoning over readily available data gets displaced by a better model. 

But 2 positions stay out of reach:

1. Mint - being in the flow when an action becomes a structured record. A vault stores value, a ledger records it, a mint creates it. Examples of companies owning this position:
@periodiclabs - they're building autonomous labs that mint experimental data (including the negative results no paper publishes) that exists nowhere else. 
@nablabio - they own the full dry/wet-lab loop; every antibody design tested against reality is a labeled predicted-vs-measured pair. 
@VinciPhysics - they're minting the verified physics record at manufacturing resolution

2. Accountability - underwriting the outcome, not just pricing it. You can't underwrite what you can't prove, so you end up owning the record itself. Some examples: 
http://mstack.ai absorbs this as the chemical supplier of record so off-spec batches are theirs to own. 
The most extreme version is owning the asset outright: 
@KoBold_Metals acquires and develops mines to ultimately solve the mineral supply gap. 
@noxmetals is producing cut metal parts through a metals service center model. 
@loombotic is manufacturing wire harnesses. 
All of these companies are not only creating data but also owning the outcome itself, and thus absorbing any potential downside risks.

One nuance: a position is only as defensible as its feedback loop is fast. When the outcome takes years to verify, you can't mint against it yet. So you find the fastest-closing loop available and mint there first. Example: 
@NOETIK_ai – they're compressing the decade-long cancer efficacy loop by using foundation models trained on human tumor biology to predict which therapies should work, for which patients -> thus not having to wait a decade for trial readouts

These 2 positions compound. Own where the data is created and the downside when it breaks, and over time you stop describing the industry's reality and start defining it.

items.text_zh:
我是在二月写下这些的。如今，它比以往任何时候都更真实。

随着实验室吸收了曾经包裹模型的脚手架，任何仅基于现成数据进行通用推理的产品都会被更优的模型所取代。

但有两个位置仍遥不可及：

1. 铸造（Mint）——当一个行动成为结构化记录时，身处流程之中。金库存储价值，账本记录价值，铸币厂创造价值。拥有这一位置的公司的例子：
   @periodiclabs —— 他们正在构建自主实验室，铸造实验数据（包括那些没有论文发表的阴性结果），这些数据在其他地方不存在。
   @nablabio —— 他们拥有完整的干/湿实验循环；每个经过现实检验的抗体设计都是一个标记的预测值与测量值配对。
   @VinciPhysics —— 他们正在以制造级分辨率铸造经过验证的物理记录。

2. 问责（Accountability）——为结果承保，而不仅仅是定价。你无法为你无法证明的东西承保，因此你最终会拥有记录本身。一些例子：
   http://mstack.ai 作为化学品供应商的记录方吸收这一点，因此不合格批次由他们负责。
   最极端的形式是直接拥有资产：
   @KoBold_Metals 收购并开发矿山，以最终解决矿产供应缺口。
   @noxmetals 通过金属服务中心模式生产切割金属零件。
   @loombotic 正在制造线束。
   所有这些公司不仅创造数据，还拥有结果本身，从而吸收了任何潜在的下行风险。

一个细微差别：一个位置的防御性取决于其反馈循环的速度。当结果需要数年才能验证时，你还无法针对它进行铸造。因此，你要找到可用的最快闭合循环，并首先在那里铸造。例如：
   @NOETIK_ai —— 他们通过使用基于人类肿瘤生物学训练的基础模型来预测哪些疗法对哪些患者有效，从而压缩了长达十年的癌症疗效循环 -> 因此无需等待十年的试验读数。

这两个位置会相互叠加。拥有数据被创造的地方，以及当数据失效时的下行风险，随着时间的推移，你将不再描述行业的现实，而是开始定义它。

